# Scout Social MCP

Lets Claude render on-brand cover images and get back public URLs. Buffer's API accepts
images by URL only, and Instagram posts cannot be scheduled without an attached asset, so
this endpoint is what makes both LinkedIn covers and Instagram scheduling automatable.

## Files

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/lib/social-covers.ts` | Renderer (satori via `@vercel/og`) plus Supabase Storage read/write |
| `src/pages/api/mcp/[token].ts` | MCP server over streamable HTTP, stateless |
| `docs/social-mcp.md` | This file |

## Setup

### 1. Dependency

```bash
npm install @vercel/og
```

Nothing else. Fonts are fetched from jsDelivr at runtime and cached in module scope, so a
warm lambda pulls them once per cold start. They must stay `.woff`, `.ttf` or `.otf`;
satori cannot read `.woff2`.

### 2. Storage bucket

Run once in the Supabase SQL editor. The bucket must be public, because Buffer fetches the
image from its own servers and will not follow a signed URL.

```sql
insert into storage.buckets (id, name, public, file_size_limit, allowed_mime_types)
values ('social', 'social', true, 10485760, array['image/png'])
on conflict (id) do update
  set public = true,
      file_size_limit = 10485760,
      allowed_mime_types = array['image/png'];
```

Writes go through `createAdminClient()` on the service role key, which bypasses RLS, so no
storage policies are needed for this to work. Public read is granted by `public = true`.

### 3. Environment variable

Generate a long random token and set it in Vercel for Production:

```bash
openssl rand -hex 32
```

```
SOCIAL_MCP_TOKEN=<the value>
```

Redeploy so the variable is picked up.

### 4. Connect it to Claude

In claude.ai, go to Settings, then Connectors, then Add custom connector, and give it:

```
https://applyscout.app/api/mcp/<SOCIAL_MCP_TOKEN>
```

Then enable the connector in the chat where Scout's social work happens.

## Auth model, and its tradeoff

The secret is in the URL path rather than an `Authorization` header, because claude.ai
custom connectors cannot attach arbitrary headers to a remote MCP server. That makes the
full URL a bearer credential:

- Anyone holding the URL can write to and delete from the `social` bucket.
- It is not sensitive beyond that. There is no access to user data, applications, or auth.
- Wrong or missing token returns `404`, not `401`, so the endpoint does not confirm it exists.
- The comparison is constant time, matching the pattern in `src/pages/api/cron/*`.
- Rotate by changing `SOCIAL_MCP_TOKEN`, redeploying, and re-adding the connector.

Do not paste the full URL into a shared document or a chat you would not paste an API key into.

## Tools

### `render_cover`

Renders and stores a cover, returning `{ slug, url, width, height }`. Pass the `url`
straight into Buffer's `create_post` under `assets[].image.url`. Re-rendering the same slug
overwrites it, and the returned URL carries a cache-busting query string.

Sizes: `linkedin` 1200x1200 (square takes more feed height on mobile than 1.91:1),
`instagram` 1080x1350, `x` 1600x900.

```jsonc
// layout "quote": a pull quote from the post, 6 to 12 words
{
  "slug": "li-2026-09-08-salary-floor",
  "platform": "linkedin",
  "layout": "quote",
  "dark": false,
  "lines": ["Decide your number", "in week one.", "Not week nine."],
  "accentFrom": 2          // lines from index 2 render in the accent colour
}

// layout "stat": one figure. `source` is required and printed on the image.
{
  "slug": "x-2026-09-08-31min",
  "platform": "x",
  "layout": "stat",
  "dark": true,
  "value": "31",
  "unit": "min",
  "label": "The average time to complete one online job application.",
  "source": "Source: Zippia, 200 largest US employers"
}
```

### `list_covers`

Everything rendered so far, newest first, with public URLs.

### `delete_cover`

Removes one cover by slug. Permanent.

## Design rules the renderer enforces

These come from `DESIGN.md` and `src/styles/global.css`. Change them there, not here.

- The mark is the official open-path glyph from `public/scout-mark.svg`, never a letterform.
  On the forest background its body path swaps to surface for the reversed treatment.
- Small accent text on the light surface uses `#49791c`, **not** the primary lime `#7fc92b`.
  Lime on `#f4ffeb` fails contrast and effectively disappears. This was a real bug in the
  first batch of covers.
- Display type is Space Grotesk 700 with letter spacing at the design system's `-0.04em`
  floor. Body and label type is Inter 700.
- Quote type size scales down as the longest line grows, so lines do not wrap.
- Text children are rendered literally. Satori does not parse HTML, so `<br>` would print as
  characters. Use one array entry per line in `lines`; `label` wraps on its own.

## Editorial rules that live outside this code

The renderer will happily draw anything you give it. These are on the caller:

- Never invent customer counts, ratings, interviews, or success rates. Any figure must be
  verified and cited, and `layout: "stat"` refuses to render without a `source`.
- Put a cover on an X post only when the visual carries information the text cannot, such as
  a statistic. Never on a thread opener, where the hook needs to be read. Most X posts get
  no cover.
- Every LinkedIn post gets one.

## Known limits

- Satori supports a subset of CSS. Flexbox and plain text work; grid, floats and most
  filters do not. Keep new layouts inside the shapes already here.
- Cold start is a few seconds while fonts download. Warm invocations are fast.
- A failed font fetch clears the cache so the next call retries rather than caching failure.
- Renders only PNG. No video, so Instagram reels still need media uploaded by hand.
